    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see where you're coming from. It's just that some people argue that if we try to over-regulate the tech to \"protect\" jobs, we'll just lose the competitive edge to other countries who aren't slowing down. In that sense, isn't the \"inevitable\" part more about the global race for efficiency? Is there even a realistic way to have policy-driven control when the tech itself is moving so much faster than the law?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
