      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that regulation kills competitiveness is a myth used to shield corporations from accountability; we can absolutely build a global competitive edge by prioritizing human capital and ethical standards over cheap, exploitative labor. The pace of technology is not a barrier to policy; it is an opportunity for us to lead the world with a more just and resilient economy. We must stop accepting the narrative that efficiency justifies inequality and instead use our laws to ensure that automation lifts everyone up rather than leaving them behind.",
      "source": "target",
